All Bosch power tools, compressed air tools and measuring tools are carefully inspected, tested and are subject to the strict controls of Bosch quality assurance.
Bosch therefore provides a guarantee for Bosch power tools, compressed air tools and measuring tools.
The Buyer’s liability for defects arising from the purchase contract with the seller as well as legal rights are not limited by this guarantee.
For these tools we provide warranty in accordance with the following conditions:
We guarantee in accordance with the following regulations (No. 2 – 7) by free correction of the defects in the tool, which are demonstrably based within the warranty period on a material or manufacturing defect.
The warranty period is 24 months, for commercial or professional use or equating uses 12 months.
The warranty period begins with the purchase by the first customer.
Decisive is the date on the original purchase receipt.
For all commercial, blue power tools and measuring tools purchased from 01.09.2004 (with the exception of high-frequency tools, industrial battery screwdrivers and compressed air tools), the warranty period is extended to 36 months if the buyer registers these tools within 4 weeks after the date of purchase.
Battery packs and chargers as well as included accessories are excluded from this warranty extension.
The registration can only be done on the Internet at www.bosch-pt.com/warranty.
The registration document, which must be printed immediately, as well as the original proof of purchase, from which the date of the purchase is specified.
Registration is only possible if the buyer agrees to the storage of his data to be entered there.
Excluded from the warranty are: parts that are subject to use due to or other natural wear, as well as defects in the tool, which are due due to use due to use or other natural use, anomalous environmental conditions, non-factual operating conditions, overloading or lack of maintenance or maintenance.
Deficiencies in the tool caused by the use of accessories, supplements or spare parts that aren't Bosch original parts.
tools where changes or additions have been made.
Slight deviations from the desired condition, which are insignificant for the value and usability of the tool.
The correction of the defect recognized by us as a guarantee is carried out in such a way that we repair the defective tool free of charge at our discretion or replace it with a flawless tool (possibly also a successor model).
Replaced tools or parts are transferred to our property.
