LokSound 5 is the most important member of the LokSound family.
Through the combination of digital decoder and sound module on a printed circuit board, we achieve dimensions of only 30mm x15.5mm and can thus be installed in almost any locomotives of track widths H0 and 0.
LokSound 5 decoders are offered with all common interfaces and always come with an 11x15mm large "sugar cube" loudspeaker and sound capsule kit.
Like all family members, the LokSound5 is a true multi-protocol decoder.
He masters the data format DCC as well as Motorola®, Selectrix® and M4.
In DCC format, 14 to 128 driving stages are as self-evident as 2 and 4-digit addresses and up to 32 functions.
Thanks to RailComPlus® the decoders register fully automatically at a suitable digitally.
It masters all DCC programming modes and thanks to RailCom® the CV values on the main track can be read out with suitable control panels.
Auxiliary registries exist for centers that can only program the CVs of 1-255.
Motorola® users benefit from up to 28 driving stages at 255 addresses.
Three more Motorola® addresses enable the triggering of 16 functions.
A built-in programming mode also enables reprogramming with the venerable Control Unit 6021.
The M4 protocol allows automatic login at mfx®-compatible control panels.
The LokSound 5 decoder detects the Märklin® braking lines as well as ZIMO® HLU braking commands or the Lenz® ABC system.
Braking with DCC brake modules or with direct voltage is also possible.
In addition, it also stops with a Selectrix® brake diode.
An ABC commuting unit allows automatic commuting between two stations.
The LokSound 5 decoder can be used on analog direct and alternating current paths.
