Omikron: Johnson wants to advance booster vaccination
Ever-new Omikron cases are worrying politics and science in the UK.
Therefore, by New Year's Day, all qualifying adults in England are to receive a vaccination offer.
British Prime Minister Boris Johnson wants to progress even faster than previously sought in the corona booster vaccinations in the face of rapidly rising Omikron numbers.
Every adult in England should already be given the opportunity to receive a booster dose by the end of the year, provided that at least three months have passed since the second vaccination, Johnson said on Sunday evening in a pre-recorded video message to his compatriots.
So far, the target date was at the end of January.
The British government will provide additional support so that the vaccination campaigns can also be accelerated in the parts of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland.
In view of the Omikron variant, one is facing an emergency, which is why vaccination protection urgently needs to be strengthened, Johnson said.
The good news is that the level of protection can be increased again with a third dose.
"Get boosted now!" Johnson said.
On Sunday, 1239 more Omikron cases were registered in the UK, bringing the total to 3137.
Compared to the previous day, this was an increase of 65 percent. dpa
