Content warning: I'm going to write something in more detail here about domestic violence.
I'll just have to write something about the soul.
(21), for professional reasons, I come into contact more frequently with the victims (and perpetrators) of domestic violence.
One topic that really gnaws at me and unfortunately happens far too often is that many victims can’t be helped or think we couldn’t help them.
It is quite clear to me that we cannot do everything and it is not perfect.
But there are fewer things in my profession that move me more than when I can’t do anything in such situations.
I see the bruises, the blood, the desperate eyes...
But even in conversation in private, with the perpetrator far out of sight and earing, I can't reach everyone.
I don’t know what’s why it’s, maybe it’s fear, fear of snatching revenge, afraid of leaving the familiar social environment, afraid of snatching the children from it.
What I always want to make clear to everyone, is sometimes very close to tears myself, everyone is worth living without violence.
I want all women to know that they don’t have to accept violence.
Often I wish I could help in any case... I know that I can't do it.
However, this will never make it easier.
Please, always remember, you are worthy to live without violence, that's so incredibly important.
