I'm annoyed by Sky Sport F1
Hello dear F1 fans, throughout the season the quality on the German Sky has diminished more and more, so I want to give myself a little air with this post.
First of all, today in the middle of the F2 race, the transmission was canceled in order to start the F1 pre-reporting on time.
Due to the delayed start and the starting accident, the schedule was far behind the planning, but you could still have shown the last (planned) ten minutes as well as the championship decision (!).
However, it seems to be the case that for legal reasons the F1 enjoys priority and therefore everything else has to be limited, so that Sky DE probably had no choice here.
Nevertheless, stupid, especially since Sky UK has conveyed the race at the end.
Nevertheless, a little praise: the commentator Olivier Zwartyes has accompanied the difficult situation about the serious accident well.
Then in the F1 there was once again an ignorance with the commentators Sascha Roos and Ralf Schumacher, so both did not know that you can change the tires under a red flag.
Although this situation already existed in Imola, Baku and Silverstone this year, both only came to the conclusion that Verstappen was allowed to change the tires when there were corresponding radio messages on Hamilton.
At Sky UK as well as RTL, both commentators immediately knew there is this possibility for Verstappen.
I am of the opinion that such elementary rules should simply be known when commenting on the F1 on a pay-TV channel.
It is also not the first guesswork, which is now possible or prescribed according to rules, both simply have constant uncertainties on the subject of rules.
In general, Roos does not like with the artificiated commentary style, but add that this is a matter of taste.
But I seriously like even Heiko water from RTL better.
In addition, there are constant sillinesses, which make both seem simply unprofessional, such as the ordering of coffee from the (also unsuspectable) reporter Peter Hardenacke or "UuuuuuHD" by Ralf Schumacher.
The latter, in particular, puts a lot of unrest in the commentary, which he apparently does not take it seriously.
Last but not least, the advertising simply prevails on Sky, in the run-of-the-run lap Sky is the only channel that goes into advertising, as you can listen at F1TV only have to make do without a commentation.
Neither ServusTV nor ORF does.
Also, these two broadcasters do less advertising in the trainings than Sky, and that as free-to-air TV stations.
Glock and Baumgartner have to be praised for their work, but that alone doesn’t make me overlook the disadvantages.
The rest of Sky Sport F1 is also very meagre and full of repetitions.
Overall, Sky is really the worst German-language broadcaster to broadcast the F1.
Unironically, RTL is doing a better job in the four races that they are still allowed to broadcast except for advertising.
In any case, the terrific F1 season is much less fun than it would be possible with a reasonable transmitter.
I'd be interested in your opinion.
