Fan pumps are ideal for supplying an aquarium additionally with oxygen.
It is also possible to operate a filtration system via aeriators.
This series is offered in 3 variants by us.
Look at the table at the end of the offer.
There you can see the services in comparison.
If the pumps are strong enough, you can operate entire plants with it.
If you have a large aquarium, pumps with 2 or more outlets are suitable, so that you can connect several outfloats.
The MK series has one, two or four outputs, depending on the model fan pump, but are also suitable to set an accent in the aquarium, e.g. with an air curtain (can be found in our shop) or with a décor that converts the air bubbles into a function.
Here you would want to mention a treasure chest, mussel or something like that.
The MK series has a special, sound-insulated construction and thus ensures low operating noise.
Installation is very simple.
The fan pump is connected by means of an air hose 4/6 mm to an outfloat or the like... and it can start.
The fan pump should be the same, or higher as the water level and mounted on the outside.
If the fan pump sits deeper like the water level you should put a check valve in between.
Simply cut through the air hose and put the valve in between.
This would prevent once water were to run backwards that the water from the basin runs through the pump...
If the fan pump is installed outdoors, it should, like other air pumps, be covered and protected from moisture
MK series pumps are pure powerhouses that consume little energy
