Extra stress before holidays & holiday weekends
This topic came up with me last week.
But now I had to use my long weekend to relax.
That's why it's only now a post.
Not only before big holidays, such as the Christmas holidays, there is a lot of stress in our company.
As it seems, there's because of holidays plus bridge days.
It was like this: Last week was Ascension, which is called "Ascent" in Switzerland.
On Friday, the vast majority of people and companies make a bridge day, which is therefore semi-official.
So there was a long 4-day weekend last week in the house.
So what happened last week?
Stress Everywhere.
Loud e-mails, which absolutely had to get out even before the ascent, order here order there, all *unconditionally* before the long weekend.
Because... yeah because?
Because "next week then" sounds like so much time and isn't allowed to be?
Or because people seriously want to do as much in a shortened week as in a normal one?
Not only was I then stressed on Wednesday, but also powerfully annoyed.
What's this self-hostaging because of holidays?
So why do we still have holidays, if we are not allowed to treat them properly?!
The stress didn’t come from above, the colleagues were all on their own.
My question is simple: Are we just like that, the Swiss?
Is that our Reforming-Evangelical manner?
Or do you know that in the north too?
