Stages in the career of new world champion Verstappen
Max Verstappen is the new Formula 1 world champion.
Max Verstappen made it.
The Dutchman clinches his first World Championship title in his seventh year in Formula 1 in the Red Bull.
His path to the top of the premier class:
Abu Dhabi - 2012, Italy: Verstappen gambles away the Kart World Championship after a crash in Sarno.
Father Jos Verstappen leaves him angrily at a gas station on the return journey.
His mother Sophie Kumpen picks up the teenager in the chasing car.
2014, England: Red Bull's junior team gets promising offspring in Verstappen.
The 16-year-old is following in the footsteps of Sebastian Vettel and Daniel Ricciardo.
At that time, he will continue to race in European Formula 3 for the time being.
2015, Australia: Verstappen starts at the age of 17 years and 166 days as the youngest pilot in history into a Grand Prix.
Due to a defect, he will have to turn off his Toro Rosso early in Melbourne.
2015, Malaysia: At the age of 17 years and 180 days, the then Toro Rosso driver Verstappen is also the youngest racing driver to score points in Formula One.
Verstappen ranks seventh at the Malaysian Grand Prix in Sepang.
2016, Spain: Verstappen wins in its first race appearance for Red Bull.
At 18 years and 228 days old, he sensationally becomes the youngest Grand Prix winner in Formula 1 history at Barcelona.
2019, Hungary: Verstappen celebrates its pole premiere in Budapest - he is not the youngest.
