The new fiber optic connection sends 500 Mbit to the FritzBox 7590 and the DLan module, which is connected to the FritzBox, they also arrive.
However, at the other DLan module, which sends out the Wifi, no longer the full 500 arrives, but the further away in the house with the module, the less arrives (i.e. use a socket, which is 1, 2, 3, etc. rooms away from the other module).
As a result, the Internet with the new fiber optic connection is now even slower on the first floor than before (\~45 Mbit).
I also ordered a new Devolo Magic set, which seems to use a new technology.
Although this was slightly better than the DLan, there were also similarly large losses.
