Often on tour and still a lot of equipment?
With the Everyday V2 Backpack by Peak Design no problem!
20 liters of capacity swallow even larger photo equipment without problems, which can be safely stowed using the padded FlexFold dividers.
And everything else you need in everyday objects, thanks to practical access in the individually configurable interior, remains well organized and separable from the photographic equipment.
With the “update” of the Everyday Line to version 2 (V2), the series also presents itself in a new look.
The chic, minimalist design has it proverbially - with the Everyday Backpack series, Peak Design has developed some highly innovative solutions that reliably protect the interior of the backpack while providing access to photo equipment in seconds.
This works with two possibilities: once conventionally via the lid flap, which can be closed with the MagLatch closure system, an excellently thought-out solution for effective protection, which has already proven itself with the messenger bags.
In the closure flap there is a closure hook made of metal with matching anchor beams at the front of the backpack.
In contrast to most backpacks, Peak Design has considered various “filling levels”: there are 4 anchor beams, stably riveted, into which the closure hook can be hooked.
If the backpack is fully loaded, you simply take the top beam, it is rather emptier, a deeper one.
Flap fasteners and hooks are also magnetic.
In this way, the backpack can also be closed reliably without locking the hook.
The second option also fundamentally distinguishes the Everyday Backpack from other, photo backpacks: In addition to the lid flap, there is also a zipper opening on both sides of the backpack.
This eliminates the biggest disadvantage of traditional backpacks with access from above - you don't have to rummage through the content anymore!
At the same time, this clever detail greatly increases the suitability for everyday use of the backpack: if you not only take your photo equipment, but also everyday items or luggage.
In the Everyday Backpack you can configure the interior individually (more on this below) and easily stow both separately from each other - and access it independently through the two side openings.
In addition, you can pull the backpack from the right side in front of the body, for example to access the camera equipment in the right compartment, for example, while the everyday things stay safely in the left half of the backpack and do not come between them.
Convenient, uncomplicated adjustable carrying straps help with this.
And since the outer shell of the backpack is also made entirely of 100% recycled, weatherproof nylon, the contents will remain dry even if it is scheduled to go to Scotland in autumn.
