Holetschek: Countries advise on elimination of the test requirement for triple-vaccinated
At their next meeting, the health ministers of the countries want to decide on a nationwide elimination of the test requirement for triple-vaccinated persons.
"We countries quickly need clarity as to whether and from when for three times vaccinated the test requirement can be dispensed with," Klaus Holetschek (CSU), chairman of the health ministers' conference, told the Bild am Sonntag newspaper.
The elimination of 2G plus for triple-vaccinated patients is "not only medically sensible, but also provides an additional vaccination incentive," Holetschek said.
Federal Health Minister Karl Lauterbach (SPD) has pledged "that he will make a proposal to the health ministers' conference next Tuesday."
