Iran sees progress in negotiations on nuclear deal
Negotiations on a revival of the international nuclear deal are looming, according to Iranian data.
"Both sides are on the verge of agreeing on the issues that are supposed to be on the agenda," Iran's chief negotiator Ali Bagheri told Irna news on Sunday.
This is a "positive and important development", because at the beginning there was not even agreement on the issues to be negotiated.
The agreement is intended to prevent Iran from building nuclear weapons.
On Thursday, Viennese talks to relaunch the agreement had continued after just under one-week interruption.
Negotiators of Iran, Germany, Britain, China, France and Russia are taking part in the negotiations.
A U.S. delegation is also on site in Vienna, but only indirectly involved in the negotiations.
Thuringia overtakes Saxony - Free State now state with the highest corona incidence
Thuringia has replaced Saxony and currently has the highest incidence nationwide.
As the only federal state, the value is above the mark of 1000.
Thuringia was the only federal state above the mark of 1000 at the corona incidence on Sunday.
The Robert Koch Institute gave the seven-day value of 1025 new infections per 100,000 inhabitants.
In Saxony, which had always had the highest incidence nationwide, this figure stood at 990.5 on Sunday.
On Friday and Saturday, the incidence in Thuringia had dropped slightly, but had also been above the value of 1000.
In Thuringia, 2242 new infections with the Sars-CoV-2 virus and 16 other deaths related to an infection were reported within one day.
200 severely ill with Covid-19 patients were undergoing intensive care treatment in hospitals on Sunday.
Reporting delays may occur on weekends.
In addition, the health authorities have been overburdened for weeks and hardly get behind with the recording of new cases.
