Advice and ideas on further professional life
Merry Christmas to you first!
My Christmas is unfortunately moderately good, because my deared head is just dismantling everything you can dismantle.
Before I come here now .. in short: I need advice and best from people who somehow know my situation - so from you.
I'm doing the ref right now as a newcomer.
Originally I studied something different and worked there also in one area (to stay at least a little anonymous, I do not mention anything more precisely here).
However, the whole thing was too boring for me and I was looking for alternatives that could be more fun for me.
At some point I landed at the teaching office and was sure that it was - even if the framework conditions are much more inflexible than in my previous profession, but I didn't care.
I've now arrived at the third "I'm googling other vacancies."
And it's only half a year around.
With the times before that, I've always decided to keep going and at least finish the ref, after which I can still pivot.
But right now I'm absolutely done.
I've had so little free time the last month that I've been completely exhausted.
It’s vacation now, but there’s still a lot of work waiting for me.
Before the ref, I always thought I was stress-resistant, but there was also my weekend my weekend and my after-work.
That's where I was free.
And the stress at work didn't matter in the moments.
Now even the family celebration is too much stress for me.
And then there are those rigid structures that annoy me additionally.
Basically, it's fun and from the outside, the ref is also doing well in terms of feedback and stuff.
But I'm completely exhausted and wondering how much stress my body endures before it shuts down completely - if he'sn't already doing that.
I wonder if I would like to have the rest of the working life - especially when I read some contributions from you here - or if I shouldn't go back into the old area, where I was valued, I could take free time when I needed it, and found the work somehow boring, but was paid appropriately and together in a team worked out and not as a lone fighter like most of the time.
But then I wonder if I didn't get back to the same place in a year as now and I'm unhappy.
You realize it’s all kind of confused, but as an outsider you might have advice or ideas on how to get out of this situation, which I’m completely finished and start crying at the slightest thought.
I won't make any decisions so emotionally right now, that probably doesn't lead to anything good.
But maybe your views will help me to see at least a little light at the end of the tunnel - or to enjoy Christmas, that's enough for me for now.
