Since its introduction in 2001, VOX's Valvetronix series has steadily evolved, leading, among other things, to the combination of advanced modeling technology with the "Valve Reactor" circuit that perfectly replicates the behavior of a tube amplifier.
With the VT20X/VT40X/VT100X Amps, we introduce a brand new modeling engine that is absolutely state-of-the-art when it comes to sound.
Thanks to VET (Virtual Element Technology) technology, which is based on the analysis of components and amp circuits, the VTX amplifiers with an authenticity that is absolutely impressive.
These amps naturally also contain the multi-stage Valvetronix tube preamplifier.
This is partly based on real analog circuits, because these get the sound variations and nuances of a tube amplifier better than any simulation.
In addition to this sophisticated circuit, the VTX amplifiers offer a closed housing and a bass reflection system, from which the natural resonances bubble.
VOX's "Tone Room" software allows you to even correct and bend historical facts on the virtual level until the amp and the effects sound like you've always imagined.
The perfect combination of tube sound with modeling technology is primarily thanks to the VOX Valve Reactor technology introduced in 2001.
Of course, it has since been refined several times in order to meet even newly added sound requirements, which once again led to a performance boost of the VOX Valvetronix series in 2010 - with more dynamics as well as more numerous and decisively improved amplifier models.
From the handy VT20+ to VT120+ with two speakers, the new VT+ Valvetronix series has also been designed in such a way that all guitarists will find what they are looking for.
All guitarists dream of the pressure and dynamics of a tube amplifier: they expect a bold sound, a nuanced reproduction of game dynamics and string stroke as well as a prompt response.
During an in-depth analysis, VOX engineers have discovered that the final stage in particular determines the tubular character of an amplifier and used this finding to develop VOX Valve Reactor technology.
The Valve Reactor circuit of each VT+ amplifier, equipped with a 12AX7 tube, perfectly reflects the behavior, subtle nuances and sound character of a tube amplifier.
