I am happy to answer questions without time limit on the organizational and human aspects and also medical questions, if they are not personally related to you (e.g. "I take medication X, this is compatible with the vaccination...").
My area of responsibility includes education for the vaccination, the indication (person is entitled to a vaccination according to coronavaccination regulations and no reasons that speak against), the medical documentation and, if necessary, the emergency care for allergic reactions (never happens to me).
Vaccination itself can be delegated to qualified personnel, e.g. medical professionals.
However, we often don’t have any with us in vaccination teams, but “only” (for God’s sake no lack of appreciativity!) pharmaceutical-technical assistants for the vaccine preparation, who can’t (may not carry out any vaccinations?”), so that I also carry out most of the vaccinations myself.
Severe "Huidlerer" question: Amberger knows the solution
What is a "Huidlerer"?
With this dialect word, sent in by an Amberger, has been provided in the BR television show "Wir in Bayern".
But unlike many previous days, the term in the "Host mi?" series remained unadvenued by the callers this time.
No, it wasn't a "man who's nervous."
And also no one, "to whom everything has to go quickly".
That, people heard from the TV presenter, was completely wrong.
On which the man from Amberg communicated the solution and thus probably caused amazement for many Upper Palatinates.
"The Huidlerer," viewers learned, "is a rage with wiping out the oven."
Dialect researcher Antony Rowley, surveyed by Bavarian television for years as an expert, confirmed this.
With the note that this is a typical Upper Palatinate term, derived somehow from the rather well-known dialect word "Houdern".
Which closed an educational gap - probably also with some who have been living in the Amberg area for a long time.
