Tyre choice in the road bike - really so puncture-proof?
This morning I woke up full of energy, because I wanted to train at least a little to prepare my bike ride in the coming week.
Said, done and I rode my road bike, which I bought on eBay yesterday.
The first 40km were also really nice - but then what lurks in such every city center (this time: thank you Krefeld!).
Shalving glass on the track.
Zack, loud hiss and my rear tire didn’t want to join the rest of the track anymore.
Since I had no real opportunity to get a spare coat and spare hose due to the day of the week, I had to turn around again with a bad mood and take home the best track.
It wasn’t that bad in terms of mood technology, maybe it’s also better if I practice with the tyre change again before the bike ride.
But now I’m faced with a question and I hope that you can help me.
Since I have a relatively long distance over several days in front of me, I would be extremely reluctant to get this problem more often.
Now it was really not bad, because also the old tires from the previous owner (very nice old man, on the day when I came to pick up the bike until 14 o'clock 120km!) and who had already described them as sub-optimal, because he drove with them for several years.
However, if I think that I still have to make a tire change when driving after 80-90kms, then I think I'm in a really bad mood :D
Now I have come into conversation with an older man at the platform, who asked me wondered why I didn’t have the Marathon Plus tyres; these are supposed to be unflatterable.
Now, of course, the whole thing sounds very tempting.
But are these really so unbreakable?
I don’t feel like spending € 40/tires now, just to be disappointed.
Furthermore, I ask myself: at the moment I have 25x622 on the road bike.
There are (apparently?) with the Marathon Plus tires, but the majority is already wider.
Is that a problem?
Or would you generally advise me on other tires on a road bike?
The Schwalbe side seems to my absolute! Lay knowledge rather to recommend the Durano DD?
Thank you in advance for the help and greetings!
Car hurls against tree: Driver fatally injured
The 53-year-old had bounced on the B57 between Rheinberg and Xanten with his car for an unexplained cause against a central island and subsequently on the oncoming road, the police announced.
There it came to a frontal collision with the vehicle of a 27-year-old.
The 53-year-old's car was subsequently hurled against a tree and the man trapped in the car.
The 27-year-old and his 23-year-old passenger were seriously injured in the accident and taken to surrounding hospitals.
